From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eugene Feinberg <uge@persimmons.ai>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 18:26:46 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 13/37] LLHD RemoveControlFlow: flatten conditional drives,
 then merge ordered drives

Two extensions that together lower the default-then-override always_comb
idiom -- CVA6's return-address stack, the hpdcache control blocks:

    stack_d = stack_q;
    if (push) begin stack_d[0].ra = d; ... end
    if (pop)  begin ... end

1. The side-effect scan refused ANY effecting op, so a drive inside a
   conditionally-executed block kept the whole region multi-block forever.
   Drives and probes are now admitted: a drive in a conditional block is
   rewritten to unconditional position with the block's PATH CONDITION
   folded into its enable ('llhd.drv ... if' exists for exactly this), using
   the branch-decision machinery the pass already had. Probes only read, and
   within one region execution reordering them past drives changes nothing:
   drives take effect a delta later either way.

2. After flattening, a single block holds the region's drives in program
   order -- and nothing downstream could consume overlapping ordered drives:
   CombineDrives groups by {delay, enable} and never merges across groups,
   Sig2Reg refuses overlapping intervals outright. Within one sequential
   block the resolution is fully defined (later drives win), so
   mergeOrderedDrives folds each root signal's drives into ONE whole-signal
   drive, rebuilding the value through the projection chains with
   struct_inject/array_inject and muxes on the enables. Array slices are
   written back element-wise via array_get/array_inject rather than
   hw.array_concat, sidestepping element-order conventions entirely.

Correctness: a reproducer with a default assignment, two conditional
override blocks and a compound-priority override (condstack.sv) SAT-proven
equivalent to its RTL at d6 through the full lowering.

On CVA6 cv32a60x this clears ras, hpdcache_ctrl, hpdcache_rtab, pmp_data_if,
decoder's combinational and more: with the companion sig2reg/deseq fixes the
design reaches ZERO residual llhd. OpenC910 unchanged, ibex byte-identical.
